            <ArticleTitle>A second look at chemabrasion.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>701-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Chemabrasion is reviewed as a single procedure in which a deep, full-face chemical peel is followed immediately by dermabrasion. In the past few years new information has encouraged some individualization of the chemical aspects of this procedure. A discussion of some factors to consider in selecting chemical agents and our recommendations based on over 5 years of experience are included. In addition, we present some useful refinements of the chemabrasion procedure.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
